            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0347" n="229" xml:id="pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.512 Stamp Tax/11</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Merrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-18">May 18, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received May 29.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 891</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s telegram
                    No. 25 of March 27, 7 P.M. and to the last paragraph of the Legation’s despatch
                    No. 871 of April 29, 1929, I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy and
                    translation of a reply<anchor n="7" xml:id="d238-f1"/> to the Legation’s note
                    making representations relative to the deposit of $50,000 required of foreign
                    insurance companies doing business in Honduras by Decree 107 of April 1, 1922.
                    As the Department will note this reply states that instructions have been given
                    to the appropriate Honduran authorities not to require the deposit in question
                    of American insurance companies or their representatives in Honduras.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George R. Merrell,
                    Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
